        "original_id": "d830f8fb-0fa5-5b30-b88d-13bc033d842c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: François de Fleury, Henry Monckton, Isaac Schomberg\n- Events: Monmouth Campaign, Battle of Monmouth, Rhode Island campaign\n- Places: Monmouth County, New Jersey, Rhode Island\n- Wars: American Revolutionary War, French Revolutionary Wars\n\nFacts:\n- François de Fleury served during the Monmouth Campaign in June 1778.\n- The Battle of Monmouth was fought on June 28, 1778, in Monmouth County, New Jersey, during the American Revolutionary War.\n- Henry Monckton was killed while leading his soldiers at the Battle of Monmouth on June 28, 1778.\n- François de Fleury fought in Rhode Island in August 1778.\n- Isaac Schomberg gained distinction in several actions during the American Revolutionary War and the French Revolutionary Wars despite his contentious nature.",
